          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "两 (liǎng) is inherited from Middle Chinese ljangX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), where it names a weight and, quoting an older dictionary, 'twice'. 'Two of a thing' grew from those senses by a step the Guangyun does not show."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
